 "notes": [
  "Source: English Wikipedia season articles ('<year> National Women's Soccer League season', league standings table) and 'NWSL Championship', fetched 2026-11-16 and parsed by script; no figures were typed by hand.",
  "Record format is [wins, losses, draws] (Wikipedia lists W-D-L; reordered here).",
  "2020 is omitted from 'seasons' and 'champions': the regular season and playoffs were cancelled (COVID-19) and replaced by the 2020 Challenge Cup and a 4-match Fall Series; neither is a league championship.",
  "2026 is included in 'seasons': all 16 clubs had completed 30 matches when fetched. It is NOT in 'champions': the 2026 NWSL Championship is scheduled for 2026-11-21. Add a 2026 champions entry once it is played. Boston Legacy FC and Denver Summit FC are 2026 expansion clubs, so 2026 is their only season.",
  "2021: Wikipedia's 2021 page also carries Challenge Cup East/West division tables; only the 24-match 'Regular season' table is used.",
  "Lineage - North Carolina Courage: the Western New York Flash franchise (2013-2016, 2016 champion) was sold and relocated to Cary, NC for 2017; it is encoded as one franchise, so the 2013-2016 Flash seasons and the 2016 title are keyed to North Carolina Courage. Caveat: Wikipedia's honours tables list the Flash as a separate former team (Courage shown with 2 titles, 2018 and 2019); split it out as 'defunct:Western New York Flash' if you prefer that reading.",
  "Lineage - Kansas City: FC Kansas City (2013-2017, champions 2014 and 2015) folded and is 'defunct:FC Kansas City'. Its player contracts went to Utah Royals FC, but neither Utah nor the Kansas City Current inherits its records. Kansas City Current is a 2021 expansion club (played 2021 as 'Kansas City NWSL', listed by Wikipedia as 'Kansas City'); it received Utah Royals FC's player-related assets in December 2020 but not its history.",
  "Lineage - Utah Royals: treated as ONE club. The Royals identity and history (2018-2020, as Utah Royals FC) stayed in Utah when the club ceased operations in December 2020, and the club that re-entered in 2024 (technically admitted as an expansion team under an option attached to the Real Salt Lake sale) is presented by the club and by Wikipedia as the same club re-established, with pre-2021 club records still cited; no 'former' Utah team is listed. Encoded as a single 'Utah Royals' key with seasons 2018, 2019 (2020 omitted league-wide) and 2024 on, with a gap 2021-2023.",
  "Lineage - defunct: Boston Breakers (2013-2017) folded before the 2018 season -> 'defunct:Boston Breakers'. Boston Legacy FC (2026) is a new, unrelated club.",
  "Renames: Gotham FC = Sky Blue FC 2013-2020, NJ/NY Gotham FC 2021-2024, Gotham FC from 2025. Chicago Stars FC = Chicago Red Stars 2013-2024. Seattle Reign FC = Seattle Reign FC 2013-2018, Reign FC 2019 (moved to Tacoma, same metro), OL Reign 2020-2023, Seattle Reign FC again from 2024. Utah Royals FC is listed without 'FC' by Wikipedia since its 2024 return.",
  "Metros: Western New York Flash played home matches in Rochester, NY (club offices near Buffalo) -> Rochester. North Carolina Courage (Cary) -> Raleigh. Gotham FC (New Jersey) -> New York. Washington Spirit (Germantown, MD in early years) -> Washington. Bay FC (San Jose) -> SF Bay Area. Utah Royals (Sandy) -> Salt Lake City. Kansas City Current played 2021 in Kansas City, KS and since in Kansas City, MO -> Kansas City.",
  "Clubs under \"inactive\" have folded but keep their history: they can be picked and ranked, and their cities are credited. Each lists the \"defunct:\" names it covers in \"names\" (its own name when left out)."
